# Trivy IaC findings to suppress.
# Format: one Trivy check ID per line.
# Add a comment above each entry explaining why it is suppressed.

# The API server is public by default, gated by cluster_endpoint_public_access. Consumers restrict
# it with cluster_endpoint_authorized_ip_ranges or set the variable to false.
AVD-AZU-0041

# cilium and kube-ovn run with network_plugin = none (bring-your-own CNI) and enforce network
# policy themselves, so the AKS network_policy attribute is never set.
AVD-AZU-0043

# The Key Vault has no network ACL by default: with a default-deny ACL, an operator applying from
# outside Azure cannot create the etcd key. kms.key_vault_network_access = "Private" is the hardened
# path, with a private endpoint the consumer provides.
AVD-AZU-0013

# The blob CSI storage account has no network rules by default: the driver reaches it from the
# nodes over the public endpoint, and a default-deny rule needs a Microsoft.Storage service endpoint
# on the node subnet or a private endpoint, both of which the consumer can add through vnet.service_endpoints
# and private_endpoints.
AVD-AZU-0012
